# Line-ending normalisation.
#
# Text files are stored LF in the repository and checked out with whatever the platform uses, so
# a Windows editor and a WSL/Linux tool can both write the same file without git seeing the
# difference as a change. Without this, one tool rewriting a file's endings turns a small edit
# into a whole-file diff that buries the real change in review — which happened here: a five-line
# checkbox edit to doc/implementation-tracking-v1.md showed up as all 397 lines changed.
* text=auto

# Binary formats git must never inspect or rewrite.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.mp3 binary
*.mp4 binary
